    "body": "Looks already fixed on upstream/main 768fe23f0: the issue's reproduction does not reproduce without a change. Suggest closing; the maintainer decides.\n\nEvidence:\n\n- I wrote an MCP test with the issue's steps. It uses 48-segment revolved STL meshes, `set_stock {from_model: blank}`, `set_raw_stock_only {on: true}`, the `Lathe` machine, the `Fanuc Lathe` post, `TN-1600-0R8`, and the Chamfering parameters of the issue.\n- On 768fe23f0, `verify` gives `\"ok\": true` for the tapered bar and for the stepped comparison bar.\n- I then put back only the sim files of commit ec2112539 to their earlier state (`solid_rest.rs`, `scan_hidden.rs`, `scan_turned.rs`). The tapered bar then fails with the issue's exact text: `finish envelope near move 1: 0.0000 mm gouge, 0.0944 mm rest`. The stepped bar still passes.\n- The issue base 58cb641ca does not contain ec2112539.\n\nLikely fix: ec2112539 `fix(turning): stop reading thread valleys and neck steps as false hidden rest` (PR #2911, #2880). It merges bare boundary crossings on non-coplanar tilted facets of a revolved 45-degree meridian.\n\nI release my claim. I did not push a branch.\n",
